1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,739
Same button. Two people.

2
00:00:02,639 --> 00:00:08,726
One of them is the chief engineer and one of them is a surgeon,

3
00:00:09,176 --> 00:00:12,220
and the hulk can tell the difference.

4
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:17,933
Last time, a choice asked what your job is.

5
00:00:18,833 --> 00:00:22,311
This time it asks how good you are.

6
00:00:23,511 --> 00:00:27,859
This is the chief's handheld, standing in the hulk's airlock.

7
00:00:28,759 --> 00:00:34,846
The bar at the top says who he is and what his job is,

8
00:00:35,296 --> 00:00:38,774
and both of those come from my roster.

9
00:00:40,574 --> 00:00:42,748
So I open my roster,

10
00:00:43,198 --> 00:00:49,285
and I give each person one new line, under their job. It's a list:

11
00:00:49,735 --> 00:00:52,778
a word, a space and a number,

12
00:00:53,228 --> 00:00:54,967
with commas in between.

13
00:00:56,767 --> 00:01:00,246
The chief is engineering four, and science one.

14
00:01:01,146 --> 00:01:04,624
The doctor is medical four, and science three.

15
00:01:05,524 --> 00:01:08,133
Now look at that last one.

16
00:01:08,583 --> 00:01:10,322
Science isn't her job.

17
00:01:10,772 --> 00:01:12,946
She's simply good at it.

18
00:01:13,846 --> 00:01:16,889
And that's what a skill is for.

19
00:01:18,689 --> 00:01:21,298
There's nothing to paste this time.

20
00:01:21,748 --> 00:01:26,965
The game reads these lines along with the rest of the roster.

21
00:01:27,865 --> 00:01:31,343
A job with no number counts as two,

22
00:01:31,793 --> 00:01:37,880
so before today the chief's engineering was two, and this line makes it four.

23
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:42,124
Here's the hulk's bridge, on both handhelds.

24
00:01:43,024 --> 00:01:48,676
The doctor has a button that the chief doesn't: pull the sensor record.

25
00:01:50,476 --> 00:01:53,954
In the file, the bridge gets that choice,

26
00:01:54,404 --> 00:01:57,013
with a new kind of condition.

27
00:01:57,913 --> 00:02:00,957
It says if, then the word skill,

28
00:02:01,407 --> 00:02:04,015
then science, then at least three.

29
00:02:05,815 --> 00:02:09,728
Dr Hale has science three, so she's offered it.

30
00:02:10,178 --> 00:02:13,222
The chief has one, so he isn't.

31
00:02:14,122 --> 00:02:16,730
And here's the thing to remember.

32
00:02:18,530 --> 00:02:21,574
When a choice asks for a job,

33
00:02:22,024 --> 00:02:25,067
and that person stayed on the ship,

34
00:02:25,517 --> 00:02:27,257
somebody covers for them.

35
00:02:28,157 --> 00:02:32,070
When a choice asks for a skill, nobody covers.

36
00:02:32,970 --> 00:02:37,752
With the doctor at home, that record isn't on anyone's menu.

37
00:02:38,952 --> 00:02:41,996
In the reactor room, a different idea.

38
00:02:42,896 --> 00:02:45,939
Both handhelds have the same button here,

39
00:02:46,389 --> 00:02:48,563
try to wake the core.

40
00:02:50,363 --> 00:02:52,537
This choice has no condition,

41
00:02:52,987 --> 00:02:55,161
so everyone is offered it.

42
00:02:56,061 --> 00:02:59,104
What differs is how it turns out.

43
00:03:00,904 --> 00:03:04,817
After the semicolon it says check, then a skill,

44
00:03:05,267 --> 00:03:07,441
then a target of nine.

45
00:03:08,341 --> 00:03:12,254
The game picks a number from one to ten,

46
00:03:12,704 --> 00:03:14,443
adds that person's skill,

47
00:03:14,893 --> 00:03:17,067
and nine or more works.

48
00:03:18,867 --> 00:03:21,476
Then else, and a second room,

49
00:03:21,926 --> 00:03:24,535
which is where a failure goes.

50
00:03:25,435 --> 00:03:28,913
And after a comma, what the party learns,

51
00:03:29,363 --> 00:03:31,537
but only when it worked.

52
00:03:33,337 --> 00:03:37,685
So the chief wakes the core six times in ten,

53
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:41,613
and the doctor manages it twice in ten.

54
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:47,296
And the page shows the roll to everyone in the room,

55
00:03:47,746 --> 00:03:52,963
so the whole party sees who tried and how close it was.

56
00:03:54,163 --> 00:03:59,815
Four rules. A skill choice is a bonus, and never the only way,

57
00:04:00,265 --> 00:04:02,874
because nobody covers for a skill.

58
00:04:03,774 --> 00:04:06,383
A check always has an else,

59
00:04:06,833 --> 00:04:09,007
and both rooms lead back.

60
00:04:09,907 --> 00:04:13,820
What comes after the check happens only on success.

61
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:19,067
And the numbers belong to the person on the roster.

62
00:04:20,867 --> 00:04:24,346
A party may try again, by the way.

63
00:04:24,796 --> 00:04:27,404
The roll is there for drama.

64
00:04:27,854 --> 00:04:29,593
It isn't a lock.

65
00:04:30,793 --> 00:04:36,446
Lint is clean, and it names nearly every slip you can make here.

66
00:04:37,346 --> 00:04:41,259
Leave the s off Skills, and it tells you.

67
00:04:42,159 --> 00:04:45,202
Leave the number out of a check,

68
00:04:45,652 --> 00:04:49,130
and it tells you nothing would be rolled.

69
00:04:50,930 --> 00:04:56,583
The one it can't catch is a skill misspelled on the roster itself,

70
00:04:57,033 --> 00:04:59,641
because you're allowed to invent skills.

71
00:05:00,541 --> 00:05:03,150
So read your roster once, slowly.

72
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:09,133
Both aboard. On the bridge, the doctor has the sensor record,

73
00:05:09,583 --> 00:05:11,322
and the chief doesn't.

74
00:05:13,122 --> 00:05:17,470
In the reactor room, they both have the same button.

75
00:05:18,370 --> 00:05:20,109
The doctor tries first,

76
00:05:20,559 --> 00:05:25,341
and the page shows her roll, with engineering nought in it.

77
00:05:26,241 --> 00:05:27,980
Then the chief tries,

78
00:05:28,430 --> 00:05:31,039
and his line says engineering four.

79
00:05:32,839 --> 00:05:35,883
That number is the one to watch.

80
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:38,941
If the chief's line says two,

81
00:05:39,391 --> 00:05:42,435
the game isn't reading his Skills line,

82
00:05:42,885 --> 00:05:45,059
and lint will say why.

83
00:05:45,959 --> 00:05:48,133
One more thing you'll notice.

84
00:05:48,583 --> 00:05:52,930
Nothing on the handheld tells a player their own numbers.

85
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:57,728
The only place a number shows is in a roll.

86
00:05:58,928 --> 00:06:01,537
Give your third person some skills.

87
00:06:02,437 --> 00:06:06,350
Add one choice that only they're good enough for,

88
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:12,017
and one check on a skill that nobody has. Then break it.

89
00:06:12,467 --> 00:06:15,946
Take the s off Skills, read the warning,

90
00:06:16,396 --> 00:06:18,570
and play it once anyway.

91
00:06:20,370 --> 00:06:24,717
Next time, one person gets a quest of their own.
